export anchor StainedGlassStyle:
    number: 152
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Stained glass
    idea: The dashboard is one leaded church window, with every panel a pane of pale jewel glass, black lead cames as the gaps between them, pointed lancets for the totals and a rose window beside the greeting.
    base: light
    palette:
        stone: #ecebe6, the wall around the window
        lead: #1b1b1f, lead cames between panes, outlines and text
        clearGlass: #f7f5ef, neutral panes, fields and progress gaps
        rubyGlass: #f8d9d9, Behind panes, the overdue notice, the activity heading and this week bars
        sapphireGlass: #d8e3f7, the header and last week bars
        emeraldGlass: #d6eedc, On track panes and the chart heading
        amberGlass: #f8e8c2, the greeting, At risk panes and the focus halo
        amethystGlass: #e7ddf5, the projects heading and a lancet
        rubyDeep: #9b1c2c, Behind and overdue text
        sapphireDeep: #1d4c8f, the primary button, the current tab and progress segments
        emeraldDeep: #1d6a3f, On track
        amberDeep: #7a5000, At risk
        amethystDeep: #5b3a8c, a spare accent for links
        muted: #4a4a52, meta and labels
    type:
        Headings and figures use Lucida Bright, Lucida Serif, Cambria,
        Noto Serif, Georgia, serif in bold. Text uses Lucida Grande,
        Lucida Sans Unicode, Lucida Sans, Segoe UI, Tahoma, sans-serif.
        Greeting 34px, lancet figures 48px, pane titles 22px, project
        names 17px, body 15px at 1.55.
    layout:
        One window up to 1240px with rounded 14px corners and a stone
        surround. It is a twelve column grid whose black background shows
        through 8px gaps as lead. Every pane is a pale glass tint with a
        white highlight in its top left. A sapphire header pane holds a
        small leaded lancet mark, the brand, outlined tabs with round tops
        where Home is deep sapphire, a square search, a deep sapphire
        button, a round bell and a four colour roundel avatar. An amber
        greeting pane spans five columns with a rose window of eight petal
        roundels beside the greeting, date and a ruby notice naming 4
        overdue tasks. Four lancets fill seven columns, each a pointed
        arch cap with tracery over a glass body with the figure and label.
        Projects span eight columns as a six pane grid, each pane tinted
        green, amber or red by status, with category, name, a ten segment
        leaded progress strip, percent, tasks, due date and status. The
        chart spans four columns, pointed arch bars in sapphire then ruby
        glass with a lead bar across, and two leaded week totals. Activity
        spans the width as three columns of panes with round initials. On
        phones every pane spans the full width and lancets go two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. The grid gap is the lead, 8px between major panes and 6px inside them, 14 to 24px padding in each pane.
    density: Medium. A twelve column window with no empty wall between panes.
    corners: Square panes softened to 3px, pointed arch tops on lancets and chart bars, round tops on tabs and swatches.
    borders: Black lead everywhere, 8px between panes, 6px under pane headings, 2 to 3px around controls and inside the chart.
    shadows: None. Each pane has a soft white highlight like light through glass.
    icons:
        Leaded shapes with a black outline. Status uses a roundel for On
        track, a triangle for At risk and a diamond with a cross for
        Behind, beside the word, with the pane tint as a second cue.
    focus: A 3px lead outline offset 2px inside a 6px amber glass halo.
    tone: Calm and plain, such as Each pane is tinted by its status.
